    "https://pacific.peopleadmin.com/postings/31054": {
      "title": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Clinical Supervisor for Teacher Education (Temporary Employee Pool) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Supervisor for Teacher Education (Temporary Employee Pool) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For Applicants Seeking Job Opportunities within the University\nInternal: Internal applicants will be considered within the first five (5) business days of the posting period.\nExternal: External applicants will be considered on the sixth (6) business day of the posting period. Posting Details Position Information Title Clinical Supervisor for Teacher Education (Temporary Employee Pool) Campus Stockton Department Benerd College Posting Number F00835 Full or Part Time Part Time Open Date 11/06/2023 Close Date 02/04/2024 Open Until Filled Yes Days Per Week Weeks Per Year Position Description Primary Purpose and Essential Functions The University of the Pacific, Benerd College Stockton campus seeks clinical supervisors to supervise student teachers and intern teachers on a part-time basis for students in the Teacher Education Program. Our current part-time clinical supervisors are drawn from regional expertise in teaching and leadership, and offer a wealth of practitioner-based expertise to our students. We are looking for credentialed supervisors for the following subject matter content: Single Subject/PE Single Subject/Math Single Subject/Spanish Multiple Subject Clinical supervisors are part-time, non-tenure-track employees, contracted via mutually-signed offer letters, to supervise specific students during specific semesters (specific dates) as outlined in the offer letter. All part-time faculty are expected to perform the following duties: Complete all employment documents and any required trainings, and submit employment documents such as signed offer letters in a timely manner. Prepare for supervision, including obtaining paperwork and evaluations that must be completed on the student, and coordination with the appropriate Director of Field Experiences. Provide an environment conducive to learning. Adhere to all University and College policies. Provide clinical supervision fairly and effectively in accordance with requirements of the California Commission on Teacher Credentialing and Program requirements. Track student attendance using tools provided, and refer students to the Hive (Office of student support services)/Director of Field Experiences if required for attendance or performance issues. Use the University’s LMS (Learning Management System) which is CANVAS , to review assignments/ IDP , post reference materials, and to communicate with students. Read submitted student work and assessments/exams, and provide written/oral/video comments to students in a timely manner to provide feedback on performance. Meet with students regularly to provide individualized direction and assessment of progress, as needed. Perform other related duties as assigned. University of the Pacific recognizes that diversity, equity, and inclusion is foundational to the success of our valued students and employees. We prioritize policy and decision-making that demonstrates awareness of, and responsiveness to, the ways socio-cultural forces related to race, gender, ability, sexuality, socio-economic status, etc. impede or propel students, faculty, and staff. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree with several years of successful teaching experience in a relevant field. Relevant content-specific knowledge and pedagogy (i.e., have knowledge of an array of teaching and learning strategies associated with the subject matter content). Knowledge of and willingness to know current Teaching Performance Expectations ( TPE ) and basics of the Teaching Performance Assessment (edTPA). Relevant Professional experiences in elementary, secondary, and/or special education educational settings. Three (3) years of teaching experience in elementary, secondary, and/or special education classrooms. California Multiple Subject, Single Subject, and/or Education Specialist, Mild/Moderate Disabilities or Moderate/Severe Disabilities credential (as appropriate). Ability to work effectively with candidates and district staff (cooperating teachers; identified administrators) in their field settings. Preferred Qualifications Prior higher education teaching experience. Ability to teach/mentor/supervise adult learners. Demonstrated commitment to and teaching in diverse settings, as well as working with students from culturally and linguistically diverse communities. Experience and sensitivity in working with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures. Demonstrated experience in advancing social justice, equity, and inclusion in a university setting. Ability to engage and integrate culturally responsive practices and knowledge in their work. Physical Requirements The physical demands described here are representative but not definitive of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Work Environment/Work Week/Travel: Travel required to various school sites where students and interns are placed. Must be able to sit/stand for extended periods. For online meetings: the successful applicant would be required to have the necessary equipment (computer and internet access) to perform the job responsibilities and would be responsible for the appropriate ergonomics of their work environment. Valid driver’s license required. Incumbent must also be able to meet the University’s fleet rules and be eligible to drive for University business. The University and its insurance carrier reserves the right to exclude applicants based on their driving record. Hiring Range $30 per hour. We consider factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s qualifications, internal equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Special Instructions THIS POSTING IS NOT A GUARANTEE OF AN OPEN POSITION . Your application will be active for 90 days. Applications are accepted on a continuous basis and are reviewed by the hiring department as openings become available. To maintain your application within the system, you may need to re-apply. Contact Information Dr. Brittany Auernig-Roan Contact Email bauernig@pacific.edu Reference Letter Information Are Applicants Required to Submit References for This Posting? Yes Minimum Number of References 2 Maximum Number of References 3 Background Check Statement All applicants who receive a conditional offer of employment are required to execute a release and authorization for a background screening. AB 810 Misconduct Disclosure Requirement: University of the Pacific complies with California Assembly Bill 810, requiring candidates accepting conditional job offers to disclose any final administrative or judicial findings, ongoing proceedings, allegations, resignations under investigation, or appeals related to sexual harassment or misconduct within the past seven years. Anti-Discrimination/EEO Policy Statement University of the Pacific is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to workforce diversity across backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints. Pacific does not unlawfully discriminate in its hiring of faculty and staff, or in the provision of its employment benefits to its faculty and staff on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, genetic information, sex/gender, marital status, military and veteran status, sexual orientation, medical condition, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, or mental or physical disability, or other legally protected characteristics or combination of such characteristics. While we strive to attract a broad and representative pool of candidates, all hiring decisions are made based on merit, selecting the most qualified individual for each position. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Resume Other Document University of the Pacific / 3601 Pacific Ave, Stockton, CA 95211 human_resources@pacific.edu human_resources@pacific.edu / 209.946.2124 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://pacific.peopleadmin.com/postings/32392": {
      "title": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Medical Assistant (Temporary)",
      "description": "University of the Pacific Applicant Portal | Medical Assistant (Temporary) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Medical Assistant (Temporary) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Medical Assistant (Temporary) Union Level Department Health Services Campus Sacramento Posting Number 201304313P Full or Part Time Full Time Number of Months 12 Work Schedule Position End Date Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants For Applicants Seeking Job Opportunities within the University Internal: Internal applicants will be considered within the first five (5) business days of the posting period. External: External applicants will be considered on the sixth (6) business day of the posting period. Sponsorship This position is not eligible for a visa sponsorship now or in the future. Position Summary Information Primary Purpose The Medical Assistant (Temporary/Casual) is responsible for assisting students and staff in all clinical and administrative support for patient care and treatment. The essential functions listed below are intended to identify those that are generally assigned. The Medical Assistant may perform many if not all functions, and in addition, other responsibilities may be assigned that are unit specific and based on business need and scope of care of the Medical Assistant. This position will be in the Sacramento Clinic but may be required to travel to Stockton and San Francisco clinics under certain circumstances. Essential Functions Performs basic clinical duties as assigned and which are within the scope of his/her practice and experience: Obtains vital signs inputs into Electronic Medical Record ( EMR ) Prepares patients for examination Assists a provider with medical procedures Educate students about health care issues and health insurance. Participate in outreach activities Administers medications as ordered by oral, intradermal, subcutaneous, or intramuscular route Performs fingerstick blood glucose checks Obtains urine and performs urine tests ordered by provider Performs electrocardiograms (EKGs) Processes lab specimens for courier pick up Performs CLIA -waived in-house lab tests (specifically, rapid strep, rapid mono, influenza, urine, pregnancy, and glucometer blood glucose tests) Administers vaccines and PPD skin tests as ordered Cleans and restocks clinical areas Orders supplies and medications for all campuses, while maintaining PAR levels Monitors inventory and expiration dates of supplies Provides general information to patients, visitors, staff and physicians. Handles and/or resolves patient dissatisfaction or concerns. Refers patient concerns to the appropriate individual for resolution, as necessary. Maintains a professional demeanor. Maintains and documents, clinical records and forms. Scans documents into patient charts through use of EMR system. Enters immunizations into the EMR . Serves as Key person for staff for Point N Click and EMR program issues. Performs basic administrative, clerical, and technical supportive tasks including, but not limited to: Schedules patients for all three campuses for Health Services Manage the schedule so sufficient sick call appointments are available on any given day Updates patient demographic information Monitor’s completion of compliance forms, collection of student health fees and confirms health insurance using Electronic Medical Record system Performs opening and closure procedures, adhering to expectations of Attendance/Tardiness policy Uses time management skills to multi-task with excellect attention to detail and accuracy Maintains working inventory of clinic office supplies: reorders as needed Performs front desk support and cashier duties for Student Health Services when needed Performs basic account/record keeping functions by posting all client transactions, confirming accuracy of the ticket, and accounting for all monies and credit transactions received for services and fees by the end of each working day. Monitors and collects outstanding student balances and no-show fees. Provides cross-coverage for CAPS and SHS administrative assistant as needed. Participate in Health and Wellness outreach activities Support Immunization compliance program Performs other duties, including participation on campus committees, as assigned University of the Pacific recognizes that diversity, equity, and inclusion is foundational to the success of our valued students and employees. We prioritize policy and decision-making that demonstrates awareness of, and responsiveness to, the ways socio-cultural forces related to race, gender, ability, sexuality, socio-economic status, etc. impede or propel students, faculty, and staff. This position serves as Campus Security Authority ( CSA ) as outlined by the Clery Act. CSAs have federally mandated responsibilities to report crimes that are reported them. Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or G.E.D. Medical Assistant Certification Completed Certification and Licensure for Phlebotomy Technician or successfully obtained within six (6) months of start date. Graduate of approved program of training, which meets state requirements to perform venipuncture, injections and skin tests, with certificate of satisfactory completion. Two (2) years’ experience in a medical office or hospital setting with utilization of clinical skills. Current BLS / AED for professional rescuers and healthcare providers. Excellent customer and communication service skills with ability to handle difficult situations with professionalism and compassion. Demonstrate knowledge of medical terminology and medical office practices. Preferred Qualifications Proficiency in medical billing and insurance claims to perform functions when necessary. Solid computer skills and proficiency with medical billing systems. Demonstrate knowledge and understanding of all State and Federal confidentiality regulations. Ability to deal with difficult or stressful situations with professionalism and calm. Positive attitude, proven ability to work successfully with diverse populations and demonstrated commitment to promote and enhance diversity and inclusion. Experience and sensitivity in working with people of diverse backgrounds and cultures. Demonstrated experience in advancing social justice, equity, and inclusion in a university setting. Ability to engage and integrate culturally responsive practices and knowledge in their work. Physical Requirements The physical demands described here are representative but not definitive of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Frequent standing and walking, occasional sitting, computer and phone use. May be requested to lift up to 25 lbs. Occupational exposure to blood borne and body fluid pathogens may reasonably be anticipated. Personal protective equipment will be provided to reduce or eliminate exposure to routine or limited infectious agents. Work Environment/Work Week/Travel Work performed in clinical environment. Work performed during standard clinic hours, may require minimal overtime to meet business needs and occasionally requires work out-of-doors with exposure to warmer or cooler temperatures. Additional evening and/or weekend hours may be requested to support department, division and University programs, projects and initiatives. Some travel may be required including to other campuses. Valid driver’s license required. Incumbent must also be able to meet the University’s fleet rules and be eligible to drive for University business. The University and its insurance carrier reserves the right to exclude applicants based on their driving record. Hiring Range Background Check Statement All applicants who receive a conditional offer of employment are required to execute a release and authorization for a background screening. AB 810 Misconduct Disclosure Requirement: University of the Pacific complies with California Assembly Bill 810, requiring candidates accepting conditional job offers to disclose any final administrative or judicial findings, ongoing proceedings, allegations, resignations under investigation, or appeals related to sexual harassment or misconduct within the past seven years. Anti-Discrimination/EEO Policy Statement University of the Pacific is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to workforce diversity across backgrounds, experiences, and viewpoints. Pacific does not unlawfully discriminate in its hiring of faculty and staff, or in the provision of its employment benefits to its faculty and staff on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, genetic information, sex/gender, marital status, military and veteran status, sexual orientation, medical condition, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, or mental or physical disability, or other legally protected characteristics or combination of such characteristics. While we strive to attract a broad and representative pool of candidates, all hiring decisions are made based on merit, selecting the most qualified individual for each position. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a high school diploma? Yes No * Do you have Medical Assistant Certification? Yes No * Did you graduate of approved program of training, which meets state requirements to perform venipuncture, injections and skin tests, with certificate of satisfactory completion? Yes No * Have you completed Certification and Licensure for Phlebotomy Technician or willing to successfully obtained within six (6) months of start date? Yes No * Do you have two (2) years of experience in a medical office or hospital setting with the utilization of clinical skills? Yes No * Do you have a current BLS/AED for professional rescuers and healthcare providers? Yes No * Do you possess excellent customer service and communication skills, both verbal and written? Yes No * Do you have knowledge of medical terminology and medical office practices? Yes No * Pacific participates in federal healthcare programs. As such, a required part of the hiring process is to verify that potential employees have not been excluded from participating in federal programs for mandatory exclusions (including for fraud, controlled substances crimes, patient abuse or neglect, or other program-related crimes) or for other permissive exclusions by the Office of Inspector General. A \"Yes\" response would be considered disqualifying. Please answer the following question accordingly: \r\n\r\nAre you currently excluded from participation in federal programs (including Medicare, Medicaid, or any other federal healthcare program)? Yes No * Pacific participates in federal healthcare programs. As such, a required part of the hiring process is to verify that potential employees have not been excluded from participating in federal programs for mandatory exclusions (including for fraud, controlled substances crimes, patient abuse or neglect, or other program-related crimes) or for other permissive exclusions by the Office of Inspector General. A \"Yes\" response would be considered disqualifying. Please answer the following question accordingly: \r\n\r\nHave you received notice that you are under review for possible exclusion from any federal programs (including Medicare, Medicaid, or any other federal healthcare program)? Yes No * Pacific participates in federal healthcare programs. As such, a required part of the hiring process is to verify that potential employees have not been excluded from participating in federal programs for mandatory exclusions (including for fraud, controlled substances crimes, patient abuse or neglect, or other program-related crimes) or for other permissive exclusions by the Office of Inspector General. A \"Yes\" response would be considered disqualifying. Please answer the following question accordingly: Are you currently excluded from participation in federal programs (including Medicare, Medicaid, or any other federal healthcare program)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document CPR/BLS Certification Other Document 2 Other Document 3 University of the Pacific / 3601 Pacific Ave, Stockton, CA 95211 human_resources@pacific.edu human_resources@pacific.edu / 209.946.2124 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
